      "side": 1,
      "message": "That was done in this CL:\nhttps://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/228834\n\nStructures do have an `EnumSet` of StructFlags (currently only used for `Block`), so another option would be add a `SpirvExplicitLayout` flag instead. That might be cleaner (and would be similar to how the logic for arrays works), but it does currently require a `const_cast` since types are immutable.\n\nI made the change as a follow up to see how it looks:\nhttps://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/230134\nThe `const_cast` is gross, but it\u0027s the same as what we do in `BlockDecoratedStructs`, and in theory these can go away if we eventually fix the const-correctness. Otherwise, I do prefer that approach.",
